LICENSE
README.md
!**/.gitignore

# Deliberately kept out of the .git exclusion above: the .NET SDK reads HEAD/refs/packed-refs to
# stamp the source revision into AssemblyInformationalVersion ("1.0.0+<sha>"), which EngineIdentity
# hashes as the build half of a worker's engine identity. Without them every image claims the same
# build, so a worker on an older upscaler build could add pages to another one's half-spooled chapter.
!.git/HEAD
!.git/config
!.git/packed-refs
!.git/refs/heads/**
test_data/

# Local-only artifacts that a clean CI checkout never has. Excluding them keeps local image builds
# representative of CI and prevents baking a developer environment (e.g. a multi-GB Python venv)
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.cache

# Databases, their sidecars and startup markers created by running the app from a checkout. In the
# container these live on the /data volume instead.
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db.bak
**/*.corrupted.*
**/.net10-upgrade-complete

# Local test / IDE / miscellaneous artifacts
**/test_env/
**/.idea/
**/.reasonix/
**/*.DotSettings.user
**/*.cbz
